  "name": "OpenVAM: Open-World Visual Attention Modeling with VLMs",
  "notes": "Static human-attention modeling on U-EYE webpage screenshots, with FIWI held out from training; no live-browser, agent-action or task-success evaluation. Gemini-generated reference rationales are expert-checked, and JScore compares generated text with references; human validation covers a separate 100-image subset. Reference text and heatmap alignment do not establish causal explanations of gaze or temporal scanpaths. Several baseline scores come from prior papers. Code/data/weight releases and licenses were not verified; no independent reproduction.",
  "published_at": "2026-09-25",
  "relations": [],
  "review_status": "curated",
  "scope": "adjacent",
  "summary": "Combines dense saliency prediction with explanations of attended elements, including webpage layouts; evaluates human-attention agreement and textual rationales rather than agent actions.",
